the flexibility of Eigen matrice's operator[],
which returns a REFERNENCE to an element:

    Matrix<T,...>

    T& operator[](size_t n) { ... }

If someone gets such a reference and changes it,
we can't guarantee any of our checks like isInverted
or isPosDef or whatever still hold.

So we'd have to change the way things are accessed
for matrices and disallow assignments like:

    Sigma[m,n] <- S[m,n] * s[m] * s[n];

Or let the user explicitly apply tests, but that has
the same problem of uglifying the models.

- Bob

